  "sourceNotes": "Version 4: the missionary role is named “LDS Missionary” in labels and instructions; spoken lines are unchanged. Lesson 1 v2: the course’s exact worksheet questions and answer key (lesson-one-exact-scenario.md, 21 October 2026), in worksheet order, between the existing introduction and goodbye. Questions are the Mormon’s lines; answers are the Christian’s single suggested response, hidden until asked for. No learning notes, evidence panels, scripture links or reading links in the help; the one passage is kept only because the content format requires at least one. Typos fixed: “bring up you’re your” to “bring up with your”, “do the LDS church” to “does”, “document” to “documented”, “firs vision” to “first vision”, plus small punctuation. Accuracy changes kept from v1: answer 1 drops the answer key’s unverified $6.1 million figure and the claim that the campaign ended the same year, and quotes President Nelson exactly (October 2018, The Correct Name of the Church: “To remove the Lord’s name from the Lord’s Church is a major victory for Satan.”) instead of saying every use of “Mormon” is a victory for Satan. Answer 4 keeps “multiple first visions” only as a question the Christian could ask, not as a historical claim; the different ages are 15 (a scribe’s addition to the 1832 account, “sixteenth year”) and about 14 in later accounts. Answer 5 keeps the course’s Church History Museum suggestion as written. The wrap-up beat uses the app’s fixed closing id “closing”."
}$scenario$::jsonb, false)
